Explanation:   In this type of question, where we   have one person work and together work done, then we can easily   get work done individually by formula
\inline \fn_jvn \frac{1}{y}=\frac{1}{b}-\frac{1}{a}
If A can do a work in x days and A+B together can do the same work in y days then B alone can do the same work in
\inline \fn_jvn \frac{1}{y}=\frac{1}{b}-\frac{1}{a}
So Son's one day work will be
= \inline \fn_jvn \frac{1}{3}-\frac{1}{5}=\frac{2}{15}
=> Son can do whole work in 15/2 days
